  by: agent  # abf8
  actor: jgstern_agent  # abf8
  clock: 5  # abf8
  nonce: abf8  # abf8
  message: "DONE, merged to dev. py.py now walks a two-hop receiver's INTERMEDIATE hops through declared return types (_chain_receiver_class_from_return_types), joining var_types + meta['return_type'] + _resolve_return_type_class rather than re-deriving any of them.\n\nBEHAVIOURAL EVIDENCE, the filed repro run end to end through 'hypergumbo survey':\n  BEFORE  calls -> TrackerSet.add   origin=method-call-recovery-linker  conf 0.50  RESOLVED  (WRONG)\n  AFTER   calls -> Store.add        origin=inherited-calls-linker                  RESOLVED  (correct)\nThe false edge is gone and the true one is in its place.\n\nPOLARITY HELD. Every failed hop is a hard stop; falling back to the last known class would stamp 'TrackerSet' as a TRUSTED hint -- the original bug from the other side. Both stops are pinned by negative controls that were MUTATED, watched go red, and restored (mutating stop 1 reddens test_member_with_no_return_annotation + test_subscripted_return_type_stays_narrow; mutating stop 2 reddens test_return_type_that_is_not_a_project_class). receiver_type_id passes the same WI-supat gate as the one-hop branch.\n\nMEASURED REACH, stated as measured and NOT as recall: 15 of 9,634 INV-mumov external placeholders on this repository (0.16%) newly carry a hint -- all 15 with a trustworthy id, and all 15 the filed instance's own Store shape. Small. The correctness win is real; the corpus effect is not large.\n\nSuite: 4114 passed, 0 failed, changed sources at 100%, mypy ratchet clean.\nUNBLOCKS WI-fihun (this row's isbefore)."  # abf8
